From 29b3a9f18476ab272a1b184a9a90f62adb0cfe0c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jr31415 <jacob@rosen4.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 12:23:58 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 10/10] Audio latency: sub-frame pushes, precise pacing,
 CoreAudio IO buffer, adaptive floor, probe

- push audio 16x per DS frame; pace with proportional precise sleeps
  (a fixed SDL_Delay(1) per chunk starves the loop)
- set kAudioDevicePropertyBufferFrameSize directly (SDL's hint never reached it)
- default queue floor 192 frames, adaptive +128 per underrun, -16 per clean 5 s
- NDS_AUDIO_TEST probe: injects a click into the real audio path, timestamps
  push and device-mix; audio_latency debug command; CoreAudio device report

Measured ~41 ms -> ~11 ms push-to-hardware on wired headphones (idle),
1 underrun across a 4,600-frame run with scene loads.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
