diff --git a/docs/audio_latency.md b/docs/audio_latency.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..3068d25
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/audio_latency.md
@@ -0,0 +1,44 @@
+# Audio latency (interactive frontend)
+
+Measured with `tools/test_audio_delay.py` (title repo) on macOS arm64, wired
+"External Headphones" at 44.1 kHz. The probe mutes game audio and injects a
+click into the exact path game audio takes, timestamping it at the SDL stream
+push and at SDL's postmix callback (the last point software sees it); the OS
+side (IO buffer + device latency + safety offset + stream latency) is read from
+CoreAudio. It is not an acoustic loopback.
+
+## Where the delay was
+
+| stage | before | now |
+|---|---|---|
+| audio batched once per emulated frame | up to 16.7 ms (not visible to the probe) | 16 pushes/frame, ~1 ms |
+| host queue floor (pacing) | 1024 frames, 31 ms | 192 frames minimum, adaptive |
+| SDL device buffer | 1024 frames | 64 frames |
+| CoreAudio IO buffer | 512 frames (11.6 ms), unaffected by SDL's hint | 64 frames |
+| measured push->mix + OS | **~41 ms** | **~11 ms** (idle), ~15 ms after the floor adapts |
+
+## Findings worth keeping
+
+- SDL's `SDL_HINT_AUDIO_DEVICE_SAMPLE_FRAMES` does **not** change CoreAudio's IO
+  buffer; `kAudioDevicePropertyBufferFrameSize` has to be set directly
+  (`nds_audio_set_os_buffer_frames`).
+- Per-chunk pacing with a fixed `SDL_Delay(1)` starves the loop (each 1 ms of
+  emulated audio then costs >= 1 ms of wall clock). Pacing sleeps are now
+  proportional to the queue excess with sub-ms precision and are skipped under
+  0.4 ms.
+- Emulation spikes at scene loads (9-15 ms) exceed a very small queue. The floor
+  is therefore adaptive: +128 frames per underrun, -16 frames per 5 s once clean
+  for 10 s, capped at 1024.
+
+## Controls (environment)
+
+| variable | default | meaning |
+|---|---|---|
+| `NDS_AUDIO_QUEUE_FRAMES` | 192 | minimum pacing floor (64..4096, 32.7 kHz frames) |
+| `NDS_AUDIO_ADAPTIVE` | 1 | 0 pins the floor at the minimum |
+| `NDS_AUDIO_CHUNKS` | 16 | audio pushes per DS frame (1 = old behaviour) |
+| `NDS_AUDIO_DEVICE_FRAMES` | 64 | SDL's device buffer hint |
+| `NDS_AUDIO_OS_BUFFER_FRAMES` | 64 | CoreAudio IO buffer (macOS), 0 = leave alone |
+| `NDS_AUDIO_TEST` | 0 | probe mode: mute game, inject clicks |
+
+`audio_latency` over the debug protocol returns the probe report.
